@baseUrl = http://localhost:5120
@token = Bearer secret-token-123

### 1. Get All Users (valid token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: {{token}}

### 2. Get All Users (Missing/Invalid Token - Should return 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token

### 3. Search Users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users?search=eng
Authorization: {{token}}

### 4. Create a New User
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
{
"username" : "cbrown",
"age" : "28",
"department" : "Engineering"
}

### 5. Trigger Unhandled Exception (Should return 500 Internal Server Error JSON)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/error-test
Authorization: {{token}}


### 6. Get User By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: {{token}}



### 7. Update User (ID: 3)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/3
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "cbrown_updated",
  "age": 29,
  "department": "Infrastructure"
}

### 8. Delete User (ID: 3)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/3
Authorization: {{token}}


### Test Edge Case 1: Create user with missing username (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "Bob",
  "age": 25,
  "department": "Engineering"
}

### Test Edge Case 2: Create user with invalid age (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "david_l",
  "age": 150,
  "department": "Sales"
}

### Test Edge Case 3: Get non-existent user ID (Should return 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/999
Authorization: {{token}}